<title>UK: World 1996/97 cotton output revised fraction lower.</title>
<headline>World 1996/97 cotton output revised fraction lower.</headline>
<dateline>LIVERPOOL, England 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cotton Outlook revised its 1996/97 world cotton output estimate down to 18.90 million tonnes in December from the 18.99 million estimated in November.</p>
<p>In 1995/96 the total was estimated at 19.92 million tonnes.</p>
<p>U.S. output was forecast at 4.06 against the November estimate of 4.07 estimate of million tonnes and 3.89 million in 1995/96. China's production was seen unchanged at 3.80 million but down on 4.76 million in 1995/96.</p>
<p>Estimates were as follows, in thousand tonnes -</p>
<p>				 1995/96		   1996/97</p>
<p>			     Dec	 Nov	 Dec	   Nov</p>
